Alright, writing index.html. Design:

- Page: light background, centered column. Header: SVG logo (gauge / personality type icon), title "Тестирование DISC", description, CTA button "Пройти тест".
- Modal (like the original): overlay + dialog, title, sub, lead, tabs (8), pane (8) each with 3 cards; progress; Назад/Далее/Завершить.
- Result screen: "Ваш результат" + formatted scores + note + Пройти снова.

Implementation details:

- Render tabs, panes from QUIZ_DATA (8 steps × 3 cards). Preserve the original aria structure (role=tablist/tab/tabpanel) — good for smoke check.
- Tabs are clickable (setStep), step is 0-7 clamp, render function same as original (is-active, aria-selected, hidden button, progress rate).
- Per-list sort via pointer events:

```js
const isCoarse = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;
function makeSortable(ul) {
  ul.addEventListener('pointerdown', onDown);
}
onDown(e):
  const li = e.target.closest('li');
  if (!li || !ul.contains(li)) return;
  if (isCoarse && !e.target.closest('.disc-handle')) return;
  if (e.pointerType === 'mouse' && e.button !== 0) return;
  ...
  el.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
  record initial coordinates, item, list, threshold 6px, dragging=false.
  move/up handlers on li (already captured).
onMove:
  if (!dragging) { if (dist>6) beginDrag(); else return; }
  li.classList.add('is-dragging') in beginDrag
  e.preventDefault();
  // find target
  const target = document.elementFromPoint(e.clientX, e.clientY);
  const t = target && target.closest('li');
  if (t && t !== li && ul.contains(t)) {
    const rect = t.getBoundingClientRect();
    const before = e.clientY - rect.top < rect.height/2;
    ul.insertBefore(li, before ? t : t.nextSibling);
  }
onUp: end, release capture, cleanup.
```

elementFromPoint: since the dragged li is under the pointer, elementFromPoint may return the li being dragged itself — handle that by skipping it. No problem.

Prevent scroll while dragging on touch: handle has touch-action:none; li may have touch-action: pan-y on mobile. On desktop li has touch-action none, but if using pointermove with preventDefault, does mouse dragging select text? user-select none on items.

Add double-click too? No.

- After completion: compute score as in the original (pos0 major, pos3 minor), then show result. In the original, the wizard closes and apruve opens; in the copy, the wizard stays open and switches body content to result view? Requirement: "после завершения теста баллы показываются в том же приложении (after test completion, scores are displayed in the same app)". Display result inside modal (replacing wizard content) — clearly "same app", and also add result below CTA on landing? Simpler: show result in modal with score, note, and button "Пройти снова" (rebuild list in original order and show step 0) and "Закрыть". Also, so page users can verify results, keep them viewable: that's sufficient.

Actually, to get closer to the original behavior (wizard closes, email modal, then result page), a clean copy would be: keep wizard in modal, on completion close modal, and show result in the main content area (where the CTA was) — "в том же приложении (within the same app)". Either is valid. Let's do: on completion, compute, close wizard, show result section on the page (scroll to it), and CTA button changes to "Пройти снова". This matches "после завершения баллы показываются в том же приложении (after completion, scores are displayed in the same app)" and is robust even if user closes modal with Esc during result display.

Wait: if in the original user closes wizard mid-test and then reopens it, state is preserved (step and order persist). Preserve this too (data stays in DOM).

- Progress: ((step+1)/8*100)%.
- Body scroll lock while modal open.
- Center active tab on small screens: implement lightweight version (scrollIntoView inline:'center' on tab on step change? that scrolls both containers...). Use a similar centerTab approach as the original. Keep it simple: on step change, activeTab.scrollIntoView({inline:'center', block:'nearest', behavior:'smooth'}) — might scroll page vertically? block:'nearest' prevents vertical jump. OK.

- Score formatting: `D:x, I:y, S:z, C:w`.

Icons: header logo uses inline SVG (gauge), check icon on result. Handle dots: use the original path (6-dot) with #B3B3B3.

Fonts: system stack. Colors: indigo (#4f46e5) accent, gray background #f6f7fb, white cards.

Handle visibility: on desktop, show handle on hover? Always subtle gray (like original; presumably in original CSS handle is always shown? unclear) — always show but unobtrusive.

Handle aria/keyboard: tabindex=0 on items, ArrowUp/Down to move, announce with aria-live? Add aria-live="polite" on list? Keep it light: tabindex=0 on li, ArrowUp/Down moves item, Enter does nothing. That's enough.

Also keep original exact tab labels: Первый, Второй, Третий, Четвертый, Пятый, Шестой, Седьмой, Восьмой. Titles: "Я наиболее" / "Я наименее".

Buttons: Назад (ghost), Далее (primary), Завершить тест (primary, hidden until step 7; Next hidden on step 7).

Close button × and overlay-click to close, Esc to close.

